ing DEFENSE_LINEUP ~84% coverage; 272-row CSV."}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:PLACEBO_DEPENDENCE"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-092", "label": "Study family SF-APPS-092: HasConn share vs pace (possessions per 48)", "score": 0.568, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-119 (0.72); FAM:SF-APPS-092 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-119", "request matches DS:NBA_play_by_play_possessions_and_reconstructed_lineups (0.74); FAM:SF-APPS-092 auto_uses_dataset DS:NBA_play_by_play_possessions_and_reconstructed_lineups"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "HasConn share vs pace (possessions per 48)", "auto_outcome_status": "not a hypothesis test", "observed_hypothesis": "Connector presence slows pace (substituting half-court organization for transition).", "observed_result": "beta(HasConn share -> poss/48)=-0.86 SE=0.38 t=-2.25 p=0.0266; within-ts corr=-0.002 p=0.782. Mix: TRANSITION -0.448 pp p=0.0013; PNR +0.980 p=0.00187; CUT +1.353 p=1.2e-11; DRIVE -0.542 p=0.0206; SPOT_UP -1.248 p=0.0003 [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Pace beta p=0.0266 but within-ts correlation is 0; no stint clock so poss/48 is period-implied. Mix shifts are clearer than efficiency.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n=28569 periods; mix n_ts=73", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "descriptive"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPS-087"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-036", "label": "Study family SF-APPS-036: Player-level BEST vs AVOID PPP gap (initiators, 55-series)", "score": 0.514, "reached_via": ["FAM:SF-APPS-015 auto_related_family (record_link_related_to) FAM:SF-APPS-036", "request matches DS:NBA_play_by_play_possessions_and_reconstructed_lineups (0.74); FAM:SF-APPS-036 auto_uses_dataset DS:NBA_play_by_play_possessions_and_reconstructed_lineups"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Player-level BEST vs AVOID PPP gap (initiators, 55-series)", "auto_outcome_status": "supported", "observed_hypothesis": "The team-level BEST vs AVOID gap holds when H2 possessions are filtered to initiating player.", "observed_result": "Mean gap (n>=10 each tier) +0.427 PPP. Mean BEST 1.347 (38 players) vs AVOID 0.920 (94 players). Stars mean gap +0.542 (n=15) vs role +0.428 (n=16). Only 3 players clear n>=30 both tiers (all BOS: White +0.864, Brown +0. [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "D_positive (no failure: positive result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Pooled player gap +0.427 in the same direction as the team gap; most star cells are below the n>=30 gate.", "observed_sample_and_power": "38/94 players at n>=15; only 3 at n>=30 both tiers", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-030", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-030: Play-type label backfill verification", "score": 0.501, "reached_via": ["FAM:SF-APPA-005 auto_related_family (limitation_precedent) FAM:SF-APPA-030", "request matches DS:NBA_play_by_play_possessions_and_reconstructed_lineups (0.74); FAM:SF-APPA-030 auto_uses_dataset DS:NBA_play_by_play_possessions_and_reconstructed_lineups"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Play-type label backfill verification", "auto_outcome_status": "inconclusive", "observed_hypothesis": "Backfilled play-type labels match expected league distributions and team identities.", "observed_result": "PNR 28.7% FAIL (band 20-28%); PULL_UP 7.9% FAIL; 3100 games with team PNR >33% FAIL; PNR PPP 0.948 PASS; temporal PASS; team identity FAIL; 2024-25 PULL_UP ~0-1% for many teams. Final: FAIL.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)", "observed_failure_evidence": "2024-25 PULL_UP shares 0.0-2.0% for many teams; 82.8% of PNR labels proxy_calibrated.", "observed_sample_and_power": "921,514 possessions", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:label_or_classification_error"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:LABEL_ERROR"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPA-001"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPA-005"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-050", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-050: Superstar sequential suppression: opponent play before the star", "score": 0.472, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-027 (0.71); FAM:SF-APPA-050 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-027", "request matches DS:NBA_play_by_play_possessions_and_reconstructed_lineups (0.74); FAM:SF-APPA-050 auto_uses_dataset DS:NBA_play_by_play_possessions_and_reconstructed_lineups"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Superstar sequential suppression: opponent play before the star", "auto_outcome_status": "not a hypothesis test", "observed_hypothesis": "A specific opponent play type on the preceding possession suppresses each star's next-possession PPP relative to that star's baseline.", "observed_result": "PUTBACK is top suppressor for 6+ stars (e.g. D. Mitchell 1.178 to 0.884, d=-0.294, n_after=95; B. Beal d=-0.345 n=32; C. Holmgren d=-0.222 n=52). Other tops: TRANSITION (A. Davis -0.058), POST_UP (N. Jokic -0.075), PULL_ [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "No multiplicity correction; n_after is 32-95 for several PUTBACK cells vs thousands of baseline possessions.", "observed_sample_and_power": "30 stars; min n_after=30", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY"}]}], "n_results": 10}

